# run artifacts: per-run evidence, never source
*.log
ledger*.jsonl
champion*.net

# Per-run ledgers and match logs: experiment artifacts, regenerated by every run.
# Zero were ever tracked; this makes that convention explicit so `git status` is meaningful.
*.jsonl
*.log
*.net

# Archived arm logs. When an arm is restarted onto a new binary the old log is preserved with a
# suffix naming what changed (.preratchet, .premates, .prehdr, .preinstr, .prev, .seed2-w1) so a
# determinism check can diff the new run against it. They are per-run evidence exactly like the
# *.log they came from — that rule already exists two lines up, but `*.log` does not match
# `*.log.preratchet`, so 13 of them accumulated as untracked noise in one evening.
#
# This matters beyond tidiness: I have been reading `git status --porcelain | grep -v '^??'` all
# session to skip the noise, and a status you have to filter is a status that can hide a real
# untracked file.
*.log.*
__pycache__/
